<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 16 July, from 622 to 1994.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/islamic-calendar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/islamic-calendar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">622 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,404 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Islamic calendar begins its first year</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The first day of the year of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hijra">Hijra</a>, 1 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muharram">Muharram</a> AH 1, corresponds to 16 July 622. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliph</a> Umar later chose the year of Muhammad's migration from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a> as the starting point of the Islamic era.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islamic-calendar">Islamic calendar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hijra">Hijra</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/997">997 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,029 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Byzantines defeat Tsar Samuel's Bulgarians at the Spercheios</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Byzantine army under General Nikephoros Ouranos defeated the Bulgarian army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> Samuel on the Spercheios river near Lamia in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. The victory virtually destroyed the Bulgarian army and ended its raids in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a> and Greece.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1054">1054 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">972 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Papal legates excommunicate the patriarch of Constantinople in Hagia Sophia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the liturgy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a>, Cardinal Humbert and his fellow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legatus">legates</a>, whose authority had lapsed with the pope's death, laid a charter excommunicating Patriarch Michael I Cerularius on the altar. Historians often date the East–West Schism from this act.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1212">1212 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">814 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Christian kings defeat the Almohads at Las Navas de Tolosa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, Aragon and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> routed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>'s army in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-morena">Sierra Morena</a>. The battle broke Almohad power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> and opened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andalusia">Andalusia</a> to Christian conquest.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andalusia">Andalusia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1232">1232 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">794 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Arjona elects the future Muhammad I of Granada as its leader</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After the final <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khutba">Friday prayer</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramadan">Ramadan</a>, a mosque assembly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arjona">Arjona</a> declared the town's independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-hud">Ibn Hud</a> and elected Muhammad ibn Yusuf as its leader. He went on to found the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasrid-dynasty">Nasrid dynasty</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-i-of-granada">Muhammad I of Granada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1661">1661 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">365 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stockholms Banco issues Europe's first banknotes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stockholms-banco">Stockholms Banco</a> began issuing paper credit notes, the first banknotes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. The bank over-issued and collapsed within a few years, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paper-money">paper money</a> was here to stay.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The first atomic bomb is detonated in New Mexico</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Trinity test at 5.29 am in the Jornada del Muerto desert proved the plutonium bomb worked. Oppenheimer later recalled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhagavad-gita">Bhagavad Gita</a>: 'Now I am become Death, the destroyer of worlds.'</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1969">1969 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">57 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Apollo 11 launches for the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Saturn V rocket lifted Neil Armstrong, Buzz Aldrin and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-collins">Michael Collins</a> from Kennedy Space Center. Four days later Armstrong and Aldrin became the first people to land on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1994">1994 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">32 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fragments of Comet Shoemaker-Levy 9 begin hitting Jupiter</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Over six days some 21 fragments of the comet slammed into Jupiter, the first collision between solar system bodies ever observed. They left dark scars in the atmosphere larger than Earth.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 16 July <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pierre-le-moyne-diberville"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pierre-le-moyne-diberville.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pierre Le Moyne d'Iberville</span><span class="tp">1661–1706</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/anderson-dawson"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/anderson-dawson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Anderson Dawson</span><span class="tp">1863–1910</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/roald-amundsen"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/roald-amundsen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Roald Amundsen</span><span class="tp">1872–1928</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ruben-blades"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ruben-blades.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Rubén Blades</span><span class="tp">b. 1948</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 16 July <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-innocent-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Innocent III</span><span class="tp">1161–1216</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-hungary"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-i-of-hungary.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles I of Hungary</span><span class="tp">1288–1342</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/anne-of-cleves"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/anne-of-cleves.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Anne of Cleves</span><span class="tp">1515–1557</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/masaniello"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/masaniello.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Masaniello</span><span class="tp">1620–1647</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/c-r-swart"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/c-r-swart.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">C. R. Swart</span><span class="tp">1894–1982</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
